WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.279
So it's not a secret that not every 2020 Democratic
presidential candidate is all in for Medicare

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:06.279
for all or

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:08.530
even for similar sort of universal coverage
proposals.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.310
And one of those people is Joe Biden.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:16.970
Joe Biden has now said more about the specifics
of his healthcare proposal.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:22.370
And it's so outrageous that more than half
of Americans straight up can't afford it.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:27.810
And what I mean by that is Joe Biden was interviewed
on who TV the other day.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.359
As many of you know, local news stations are
crazy about copyright.

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:34.090
So I'm not going to play any clips for you,
but you can easily find the interview online

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.090
and check it out in full.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.880
And in this interview with the TV station,
Joe Biden says that his approach is not a

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:47.190
Bernie Sanders ask Medicare for all approach,
which we knew it's building on Obamacare.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:53.010
And Biden specifically says that he wants
to further subsidize private insurance, which

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:58.210
is completely broken, of course, in order
to reduce yearly copays to $1,000.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:04.780
So for context, a lot of the plans that Biden
is talking about have $2,000 a year of copays

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.299
or a, I'm sorry, uh, deductibles.

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:10.210
I said, I think I said a copay, but I mean
deductible.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:16.670
He wants to reduce to $1,000 deductible plans
that right now might have a $2,000 deductible

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.640
or a $2,500 deductible.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.310
And he's also open to a public option.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:26.290
And the primary problem with all of this is
that it's completely unaffordable for hundreds

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.159
of millions of people and it doesn't actually
address the real issues with our healthcare

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:32.159
system.

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:34.319
And I'll explain to you both of those points.

00:01:34.319 --> 00:01:39.380
You might remember that a few months ago we
did a story about a study which found that

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:47.469
presented with an unexpected $400 emergency
expense, 40% of the country can't afford it.

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:52.299
And by can't afford it, it means they either
would have to take out a loan or go into debt,

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:58.069
charge it, uh, and pay it off at interest
or borrow from family or get a payday loan.

00:01:58.069 --> 00:02:02.789
Imagine, which is the worst opportunity, a
possibility in order to cover the unexpected

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.499
$400 expense.

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:12.000
Joe Biden is saying, I will further subsidize
insurance in order to reduce the yearly deductible

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:20.590
from whatever it is, 2,500 to 32,000 sometimes
even more down to $1,000 out of pocket Max

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:27.580
if 40% can't afford an unexpected $400 expense,
and then certainly more than half of the country

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:36.780
can't afford $1,000 deductible above and beyond
premiums and medications and so on and so.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.280
Now what this also ignores of course is the
cost of the plans themselves.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:47.300
Biden's talking just about lowering the deductible
to $1,000 and then Biden ads, I guess sort

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:53.280
of like as a wink wink or an attempt to bring
in some of the people who understand how broken

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.900
our healthcare system is.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.020
Biden says that he's also open to a public
option and sure, a public option is a fine

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:04.700
idea if you are comparing between what we
have now and what we have now plus a public

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.700
option.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.470
Sure, I'll take the public auction option,
but a congressional budget office study found

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:15.310
that a public option would basically only
lower monthly premiums by seven to 8%.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.760
This barely makes a dent, especially when
you consider how quickly premiums are going

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.640
up year after year.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.650
Biden also repeats in this interview, what
is basically a Republican talking point, which

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:29.740
is that under Bernie Sanders, medicare for
all plan, you would lose your insurance.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.940
It's incredibly dishonest.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.060
It's not true.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.110
The way it would work is a public option would
be put in place immediately during the four

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:41.640
year phase in to Medicare for all during which
the uh, age for Medicare eligibility gets

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.460
lowered and lowered until everybody is in
to say you lose your insurance under Bernie's

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:53.450
plan is incomplete at best and completely
dishonest and a Republican talking point at

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:54.450
worse.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.890
Th th this is the worst part of Joe Biden.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:04.050
These are Republican for profit health insurance
company talking points and Joe Biden is repeating

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.050
them.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.830
Now I will, you know, try to find some kind
of silver lining here.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:13.100
The one thing I appreciate about Joe Biden
is he's being upfront with us.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.239
He's not for Medicare for all and he's telling
us he's not for Medicare for all.

00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:18.239
We can debate it.

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:20.100
We can discuss whose plan is the best.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.210
We can discuss whose plan would be best for
low income, middleware, whatever.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.860
Joe Biden is not playing coy the way that
Kamala Harris did.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.680
We're on a CNN town hall town hall.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:34.610
She said Medicare for all is the way and then
the next day put out a statement saying Medicare

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:39.930
for all would be one way and tweaking Obamacare
is another way that I would also be open to

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.370
Joe Biden has been upfront.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.819
He's not for Medicare for all.

00:04:43.819 --> 00:04:48.199
He's been up front with the wealthy donors
behind closed doors, but it went public saying

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:52.759
you're privileged status will remain on changed
if I become president of the United States.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.020
He is safe for the super rich.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.020
He's been upfront.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.310
I don't agree with Biden's politics.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:04.509
I think it's terrible, but he is not sugarcoating
it to appear more progressive than he is and

00:05:04.509 --> 00:05:08.759
we can actually evaluate it for what it actually
is rather than having to read between the

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:11.379
lines and what my assessment is.

00:05:11.379 --> 00:06:26.659
Is that it's horrible and I completely disagree
with it.

